## Agent skills

### Issue tracker

Vikunja (service `tasks`), project `{{ name }}`; commits and PR bodies end with `Task: tasks#<id>`. See
`docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`.

### Triage labels

The five default roles (`needs-triage`, `needs-info`, `ready-for-agent`, `ready-for-human`, `wontfix`) as Vikunja
labels. See `docs/agents/triage-labels.md`.

### Domain docs

Single-context: `GLOSSARY.md` (in place of `CONTEXT.md`) and `docs/adr/`, both created by `/domain-modeling` once a
term or decision is settled. Use the glossary's words in code, tickets and commits; platform terms (service, gateway,
schema, actor, audit, ...) are defined in homelab-common's
[GLOSSARY.md](https://github.com/navaneethkrishna30/homelab-common/blob/main/GLOSSARY.md), not here. Read the ADRs
touching your area and flag any you contradict. See `docs/agents/domain.md`.
